Subject: Chronos Drift - Urgent Transmission

Agent Kepler,

Received your encoded burst regarding the anomaly at Sector Gamma-9. Confirmed. The temporal distortions are escalating beyond predicted parameters. Initial scans suggest it’s not a natural phenomenon – the energy signature doesn’t match any known stellar event, or even the Xylosian resonance we’ve been monitoring. It’s… constructed. Deliberately.

My team has managed to isolate the source – a derelict research station, designation ‘Kairos’, orbiting the gas giant Xylos Prime. Records, fragmented as they are, indicate Kairos was a joint venture between the Precursors and the now-vanished Cygnus Collective, focused on manipulating localized spacetime. They were attempting to create ‘temporal anchors’ – points of stability within the chaotic currents of the Chronos Stream. Apparently, they failed. Spectacularly.

The distortion isn’t a simple ripple, Kepler. It’s a *fracture*. A tear in the fabric of time, leaking echoes of… possibilities. We’ve detected brief, fragmented projections – glimpses of alternate timelines. Some benign, others… deeply unsettling. One showed a version of Earth consumed by a crystalline plague. Another, a galactic empire ruled by sentient fungi. I’m not exaggerating.

The primary concern isn’t the visions themselves, but the *bleed-through*. Objects, energy signatures, even *lifeforms* are momentarily phasing in and out of our reality. We’ve already lost two operatives to what we’re calling ‘temporal displacement’ – they simply ceased to exist, overwritten by echoes from other timelines. 

I’ve dispatched a reconnaissance drone equipped with a Chronos Dampener – a prototype device designed to stabilize localized temporal fields. It’s a long shot, but it might buy us some time. However, the Dampener requires a rare isotope, Xylosian Crystone, to function at full capacity. Your sector is the only known source. 

I need you to divert all Crystone shipments to my location – designated Outpost Echo-7. Prioritize this above all other directives. The fate of multiple realities may depend on it. 

Be warned, Kepler. The distortions are affecting communications. Expect signal degradation and potential message scrambling. Use the tertiary encryption key – Omega-9 – for all future transmissions. And for the love of all that is stable, avoid direct exposure to the anomaly. We don’t know what’s on the other side, and frankly, I don’t want to find out.

Report any unusual activity in your sector immediately. This isn’t just a mission anymore, Kepler. It’s a containment breach.

Agent Lyra.
Outpost Echo-7.
End Transmission.



